   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT creating the Starr public library district in the town of Rhinebeck, New York; and to amend chapter 672 of the laws of 1993 amending the public authorities law relating to the construction and financing of facilities for certain public libraries, in relation to including the Starr public library district within the provisions of such chapter and providing for financing through the dormitory authority",
    "basePrintNo": "S5500",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5500-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §5, Chap 672 of 1993",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5500\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act creating the Starr public library district in the town of\nRhinebeck, New York; and to amend chapter 672 of the laws of 1993\namending the public authorities law relating to the construction and\nfinancing of facilities for certain public libraries, in relation to\nincluding the Starr public library district within the provisions of\nsuch chapter and providing for financing through the dormitory\nauthority\n\nPURPOSE:\n\nTo create the Starr public library district in the Town of Rhinebeck\nand provide for the election of the board of trustees as well as the\nmeans for construction and financing of facilities and operations\nwithin the district\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 creates the library district.\n\nSection 2 outlines the election procedures for the board of trustees.\n\nSection 3 details the procedure for determining the term length of\neach trustee; filling vacancies in the board; appointing a board\npresident, vice president, and secretary as well as any other\npositions the board deems necessary such as treasurer.\n\nSection 4 explains the financial obligations and procedures for the\nlibrary district to establish a budget, make payments, and collect\nfunds. This section also establishes a treasurer as the overseer of\nall funds with the board auditing and approving all final payments and\nclaims once they have had the opportunity to review an itemized record\nof the payment or claim.\n\nSection 5 sets procedures for its charter from the board of regents,\ncommencement of operations,and transfer of property and employees.\n\nSection 6 provides for an ad valorem levy which means the tax\ncollected will be based on the value of the real estate or personal\nproperty within the Town of Rhinebeck, given that property within the\nTown of Rhinebeck will benefit from the library facilities being\nestablished and maintained.\n\nSection 7 clarifies that except as: otherwise provided by this act,\nthe provisions of the education law relating to public libraries shall\nbe applicable to the library district established by this act.\n\nSection 8 deems the public library district separate and distinct from\nthe town for all purposes, including but not limited to management,\nappropriations, and expenditures\n\nSection 9 adds a new subdivision 49 to section 5 of chapter 672 of the\nlaws of 1993.\n\n\nSection 10 sets an immediate effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nFounded in 1862, the Starr Library in Rhinebeck has been serving\npatrons in the Mid-Hudson Valley for over 150 years. It is the oldest\nlibrary in the Mid-Hudson library system and has an incredible history\nof being an important educational resource.  Originally located in the\nStarr Institute Building in Rhinebeck, the library moved up to West\nMarket Street in the 1970s. In 2005, they had outgrown their smaller\nbuilding and the Board of Trustees raised the funds to construct a new\nwing, which expanded their offerings to the community.\n\nThe creation of the Starr public library district is the next step\nforward for this important institution to continue its important work\nin providing educational resources for residents in the Rhinebeck\ncommunity and throughout the Mid-Hudson Valley.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2013-2014: S.7259-A - Vetoed, Memo.509\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
